# Local-only working proposals and analyses. These are team-internal planning
# notes, not part of the framework's public surface. The rationale that
# survives into the framework lives in docs/methodology.md, the ADRs, and the
# rest of the public docs - not here. Root-anchored for the same reason as
# the patterns below.
/docs/proposals/
/docs/analysis/

# Compass per-project working state.
#
# IMPORTANT - in a real project that USES Compass, `.compass/work/` IS
# committed: it is the audit trail (manifest.yml, devlog.md, evidence/).
# Only the framework repo itself ignores its own root-level `.compass/work/`,
# and the patterns below are ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading `/` so they do not
# also exclude `examples/<x>/.compass/work/...` - those ARE part of the
# repo and must be tracked. (Without the leading `/`, git matches the
# pattern at any depth, which silently drops the examples.)
/.compass/work/
/.compass/flow/
/.compass/current-task

# The framework's own issue documents, relocated out of `.compass/work/` by
# `compass migrate`. Same rule as the patterns above and for the same reason:
# in a project that USES Compass these ARE committed - they are the audit
# trail a reviewer opens - and only the framework repo ignores its own.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED, so `examples/<x>/docs/compass/...` stays tracked. Those
# documents are shipped surface: an adopter reads them to learn the pipeline.
#
# The two hand-written files sitting flat in `docs/compass/` are already
# tracked and stay tracked - `.gitignore` does not affect a tracked file.
# They are not an issue's record: one is a cross-issue intake, the other a
# spike conclusion.
/docs/compass/*/

*.log

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
__MACOSX/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python / pytest
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.mypy_cache/

# Backups (e.g. from `sed -i.bak`)
*.bak

# Node (if a project uses it)
node_modules/

# Release artifacts (root only - a project that vendors Compass may legitimately
# have its own dist/ or build/ elsewhere).
/dist/
/build/
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# Local editor/tool MCP server config. Points at a port on one developer's
# machine, so it is never shareable.
/.mcp.json

# evals/harness.py's run records - one per scenario, condition and run
# number. The pilot's own report is the published result, not these.
/evals/out/

# BDD reference adapters install their own dependencies; an adopter runs the
# README's setup step, and CI does the same. Committing them would make the
# examples heavier than the framework.
examples/bdd-adapters/*/node_modules/
examples/bdd-adapters/*/features/*.feature
examples/bdd-adapters/*/.compass/work/*/spec.feature
examples/bdd-adapters/*/.compass/work/*/acceptance-criteria.feature
